{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And if men quarrel.</b> Why is this said? Since 'eye for eye' was stated, we learned only the damages for his limb, but idleness and healing we did not learn — therefore this section was stated." "<b>and he falls to his bed.</b> As its Targum renders: וְיִפֵּל לְבוּטְלָן — to an illness that incapacitates him from his work."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:34.722652555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}